course: dictionary
lesson: 10393
title: The triangle: shape, sound and sign
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A triangle is a flat shape with three straight sides and three corners. The corners are called angles. So a triangle always has 3 sides and 3 corners.
explain: Triangle is also a word for a musical instrument: a metal bar bent into a triangle, which you hit with a small rod. And anything shaped like a triangle can be called a triangle, like a slice of pizza or a warning sign. Read the words around it to know which meaning is meant.
explain: «A triangle frame keeps its shape when pushed, but a square frame can be pushed out of shape.» The words frame and pushed tell you this triangle is the flat shape, and that a triangle is stiff and holds its shape.
explain: «To count the sides of many shapes, multiply each kind by its number of sides and add.» Here the sentence is about counting, so triangle must mean the shape. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners, called angles.
fact: The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of its three sides.
fact: The angles in any triangle add up to 180 degrees.
fact: Triangles can be equilateral (all sides equal), isosceles (two sides equal) or right-angled.
fact: Pythagoras studied triangles, and «the fire triangle» shows three things that work together.
exercise: «To count the sides of many shapes, multiply each kind by its number of sides and add.» How many sides do 2 triangles and 3 squares have? | 15 | 20 | *18 | 12
exercise: How many corners does a triangle have? | *3 | 5 | 2 | 4
exercise: In a triangle, the angles add up to how many degrees? | *180 | 360 | 270 | 90
test: A metal bar bent into a triangle, which you hit with a small rod, is called a what? | A bell | *A triangle | A tambourine
test: A triangle with two equal sides is called what? | Circular | Pentagon | Equilateral | *Isosceles
exam: «Heat, fuel and oxygen are called the fire triangle.» What does triangle mean here? | A musical instrument | A warning sign on a road | *Something shaped like a triangle, a picture of three linked things | A type of toad
